  "evaluation": "All three responses correctly identify this as a genuine conflict primarily driven by population differences (older CKD patients vs middle-aged psychiatric patients and healthy controls). Response B is the most disciplined in its `also_differs` field, noting only `outcome_measure` (WHO CIDI-SF vs treated depression status) and `design_or_bias` (adjusted cross-sectional analysis of a deficiency cutoff vs unadjusted case-control comparison of continuous serum levels). Responses A and C unnecessarily include `comparator`, which here is simply an artifact of how the case-control and cross-sectional study groups were extracted rather than an independent treatment comparator difference. Between C and A, C has a slightly clearer rationale and detail format.",
